On 3 Oct 2006 09:49:31 -0700, Displaced Avenger wrote:

>My wizard is expert in dagger, expert in attack spells, and skilled in
>all other spells.  He still has several skill slots available.  Is
>there any benefit to taking spell classes to expert, other than casting
>failure rates?  Currently, the only spell he can't cast at 0% is
>cancellation, which doesn't seem worth the bother.
>
>According to <http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/343/spl2-343.html>,
>some spells become more effective/behave differently when you go from
>basic to skilled (fireball, for instance).  But the only spell which
>seems to get tweaked from skilled to expert is jump, which gains a
>little distance.
>
>Am I missing something?  

  Probably a +5 fireproof small shield.  Finger of Death with a small
shield is 32% failure at Skilled, 0% failure at Expert.

>Do I need these extra skill slots for spells,

  For Attack (see above) and Escape for the spell of jump definitely
yes.  That extra jump square is a godsend on Astral.  Few monsters are a
threat when they're rapidly receding in your rear view mirror.

  You may want it for other spell schools once you try on a small
shield.  Maybe even Clerical for the failure rate of spell of
protection.  

  Sure, it's "only" 4-5 points of AC.  If you had a +4 ring of
protection, would you wear it?  What if it didn't take a ring slot?

  Add the +6 from the +5 small shield to the +4 from the spell of
protection and that drops your AC by 10 points.  Think of it as getting
to wear an extra set of Dragon Scale Mail.

>or should I just play around with them?
>

  Do both.  Expert spell of jump lets you jump 3 squares diagonally, 4
squares in a straight line.  That's a 25% increase.  Not much compared
to controlled teleport, but awesome on the Plane of Fire and the Astral
Plane.  It's like being pushed by angels.  

  For completely unlit areas you'll need the Candelabrum of Invocation
to let you see far enough to take advantage of the extra distance.

  Did I mention that the spell of jump works no matter what your
burdened status is?
  

  I'd try Ascending a full-up Wizard with all spells, every spell skill
maximized, maximum armor, and casting every spell when and as
appropriate.  That's playing around as a Wizard.  



